These experiments are deliberately **limited** in scope:

A.Only one participant per dataset was examined; the results cannot establish generalization to unseen people.
B. Hyser provides individual finger forces, not direct thumb index contact force.
C. CEMHSEY GESTURE provides gesture labels but no measured force.
D. The analysis covers selected experimental tests rather than the complete physiological framework.
E. Learned neural drive representations, incontext personalization and the complete real-time robotic pipeline remain proposed research directions.
F. Cross trial and cross day comparisons are useful preliminary checks, but do not establish clinical or robotic deployment performance.

The repository is intended to demonstrate my experimental reasoning.
